Demote config values in the style build only

The config dialog compiles config_file.cpp with CONFIG_DIALOG, and four
classes of value demotion run in that build as well as in the style
build. Nine appearance combos offer Raised or Bevelled, which the reader
rewrites to Flat or Standard gradient. Each appearance combo offers 23
custom gradients, where the defaults define two, and the reader rewrites
an undefined one to the general appearance. The slider width spin box
takes five and seven, where the reader clears the thin groove box. The
group box shade factor takes zero, where the reader turns the shaded
frame into a plain one. A reopened dialog therefore shows a value the
user never chose, and the next Apply writes that value over the file.

Run each demotion in the style build alone, beside the Agua rewrites
that already sit there. The style keeps the render it has today, the
file and the dialog keep the stored value, and the round trip closes.

Give tbarBtnAppearance the custom gradient check that the other 23
appearance fields hold. Without the check an undefined gradient reaches
qtcGetGradient, which answers the raised form in place of the general
appearance.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 12 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

